// A source at a stated cadence puts bodies in on the ticks it promises.
//
// **The golden trace is the assertion, not the count.** `enemy_count: 4` says
// four bodies arrived and cannot say when; the trace says tick 0, 10, 20 and
// 30, which is the whole claim. A source that started cold rather than ready
// would produce the same four bodies one cadence later and satisfy every other
// line in this file.
//
// `fired` and `placed` are both there on purpose: one says which source asked,
// the other says a body appeared. With one source they are redundant; with two
// they are the only way to tell whose output is whose.
//
// The template rides along — the source makes chasers, so `seekers: 4` says the
// grants flow through a source exactly as they do through a direct placement.
// Thirty units out at 3.5 units/sec, none of them gets anywhere near the player
// inside the budget, so nothing here is about the solver.
(
    description: "A source at every=10 fires on ticks 0, 10, 20 and 30, and what it makes chases.",
    setup: (
        sources: [
            (pos: (30.0, 0.0), radius: 3.0, every: 10, what: (seeks: true)),
        ],
    ),
    inputs: [],
    budget: (ticks: 31),
    expect: (
        player_pos: (x: 0.0, z: 0.0, tol: 0.0001),
        enemy_count: 4,
        seekers: 4,
        sources: 1,
        contacts: 0,
        crowd_contacts: 0,
        trace: "a_source_fires_on_the_ticks_it_promises.trace",
    ),
)
